==Old English==

===Etymology===
''Tiwes'' (''genitive'' of [[Tiw|Tīw]]) + [[dæg|dæġ]] (corresponding to {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*Tīwas dagaz}}). Cognate with {{cog|ofs|Tiesdei}}, {{cog|goh|zīostag}} (dialectal German ''Zistig''), {{cog|non|týrsdagr}}/{{m|non|týsdagr}} ({{cog|sv|tisdag}}). Used in translation of the Latin ''[[dies Martis]]''
{{PIE root|ang|dyew}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtiwezdæj/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|m|head=tiwesdæġ}}

# [[Tuesday]]

